---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { t } from "../lib/i18n";
const ui = t("en");
---
<Base lang="en" title={ui.contributeTitle} description={ui.contributeDek} path="/contribute">
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow contribute" style="padding:1.4rem 0 2.5rem">
    <p class="kicker">{ui.siteKicker}</p>
    <h1>{ui.contributeTitle}</h1>
    <p class="dek">{ui.contributeDek}</p>
    <p>{ui.creditLine}. This glossary is open-source educational material. It is not legal advice.</p>

    <h2>What belongs here</h2>
    <p>Add or improve terms used in mortgage origination, underwriting, disclosure, or servicing. Every entry needs a plain-language definition, an illustrative file or form example, at least one primary-source citation (a regulation, statute, or agency guide), and a Spanish rendering that follows CFPB terminology where the Bureau has published a term.</p>

    <h2>Data format</h2>
    <p>Each term is one JSON file at <code>src/content/terms/{"{slug}"}.json</code>. Required fields:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>term</code>, <code>aliases</code>, <code>category</code>, <code>definition</code>, <code>details</code>, <code>complianceNotes</code></li>
      <li><code>example</code> with <code>setting</code> and <code>text</code></li>
      <li><code>citations</code> (ids from <code>src/data/citations.json</code>)</li>
      <li><code>related</code> (other slugs; the validator makes links bidirectional)</li>
      <li><code>reviewed</code> (ISO date) and a matching <code>es</code> object with the same structure</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Categories: <code>origination</code>, <code>underwriting</code>, <code>compliance</code>, <code>closing</code>, <code>servicing</code>, <code>loan-programs</code>, <code>borrower-faqs</code>.</p>

    <h2>Citation requirements</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Cite the official text, not a blog post or a secondary explainer, unless you are also pointing to the official source.</li>
      <li>Prefer eCFR, the U.S. Code, CFPB regulations and interpretations, and current Fannie Mae, Freddie Mac, FHA, VA, or USDA guides.</li>
      <li>Do not invent section numbers, dollar thresholds, or deadlines. If a figure changes every year, cite the source and do not hard-code the number in the example. Mark examples with the words “Example figures” (English) or “Cifras de ejemplo” (Spanish).</li>
      <li>Do not present this site as affiliated with the CFPB, Fannie Mae, Freddie Mac, HUD, VA, or USDA.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to add or edit a term</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Add the slug to <code>scripts/reference_data.py</code> and run <code>npm run data</code>.</li>
      <li>Create or update the JSON file, including the <code>es</code> object.</li>
      <li>Run <code>npm run validate</code>. Fix any missing citations, broken related links, or incomplete Spanish fields.</li>
      <li>If you can, also run <code>npm run check:es</code> and <code>npm run check:links</code>.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Review process</h2>
    <p>Entries are reviewed against the cited source and for plain language in both English and Spanish. Spanish that follows a published CFPB term should keep that wording unless a reviewer notes a reason to depart. Spanish that has not had a native-speaker legal review should stay flagged as such. Shaun Barry, NMLS #30170, reviews substantive compliance wording before an entry is treated as final.</p>
    <p>The source is public at <a href="https://github.com/XBitcoinBytes/mortgage-compliance-glossary">github.com/XBitcoinBytes/mortgage-compliance-glossary</a>. Open a pull request with your change and a short note on the source you used. You can also reach Shaun through the <a href="https://shaun-barry-portfolio.vercel.app">portfolio site</a>. Do not submit real borrower data or non-public loan files.</p>

    <h2>Local preview</h2>
    <pre><code>npm install
npm run dev</code></pre>
    <p>The dev server listens on http://127.0.0.1:4327.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
